85 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 72 0 R
/T (Simply put: imagine you have a bunch of sensors \(radars, cameras\) that detect moving targets \(cars, people\), but the data is noisy, conflicting, and duplicated. Algorithms decide how to "clean" it up and track it correctly, and entropy acts as a mathematical "chaos thermometer" to honestly evaluate how well the algorithms performed.)
/E (Simply put: imagine you have a bunch of sensors \(radars, cameras\) that detect moving targets \(cars, people\), but the data is noisy, conflicting, and duplicated. Algorithms decide how to "clean" it up and track it correctly, and entropy acts as a mathematical "chaos thermometer" to honestly evaluate how well the algorithms performed.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
